expr main <([has, have, had] [already, just, never, ever, still] took), (took)>

let message "Use the past participle `taken` here."
let description "After `have`, `has` or `had`, the verb needs its past participle: `taken`."
let kind "Grammar"
let becomes "taken"
let strategy "MatchCase"

test "She has already took it." "She has already taken it."
test "She have just took it." "She have just taken it."
test "She had never took it." "She had never taken it."
test "She has just took it." "She has just taken it."
test "She have already took it." "She have already taken it."
test "She had already took it." "She had already taken it."
test "She has never took it." "She has never taken it."
test "She have never took it." "She have never taken it."
test "She has still took it." "She has still taken it."
test "She had just took it." "She had just taken it."
test "She have ever took it." "She have ever taken it."
test "She has ever took it." "She has ever taken it."
test "They have already took twice." "They have already taken twice."

allows "She has already taken it."
allows "They have just taken it."
allows "She took it yesterday."
allows "He already took it."
allows "We never took it."
allows "She has finished."
